WEBVTT

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.060
Fields of green grass.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.850
Well, mold is, uh, is green.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.700
Crystal blue streams.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.120
Raptured bile ducts, actually.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.840
If I had anything at all in my stomach right now, I'd throw up.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.030
Oh, wow.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.350
Never seen anything like it.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.320
Maya could fit in its mouth.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.120
It's the remains of a budok.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.970
One of the largest creatures ever.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.340
Last month, you've been telling us about this fantastic place where we're gonna get fed.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.860
And this is it? A big, rotting budong!

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.480
You mean, that thing's edible?

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.020
A budong flesh is what's kind of poisonous.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:48.210
It's got these pustule things filled with acid mucous.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:51.230
Yeah, yeah, yeah. We got it. We got that one. It ain't edible.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.460
What's the matter with you?

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.620
I don't know. I don't know. I hope it's not a cold.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.690
I'm sure you're not gonna get any chicken soup on a boudon.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:05.710
Look, I don't know what chicken soup is, okay?

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.990
But there's plenty of other food at the mining camp.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.130
What, people live on a boudon?

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:15.180
Inside, yeah. Mining for nigelti crystals.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.420
How'd you find out about this fix?

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.500
My brother Neri and I stayed here for a while.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:22.790
We had a great time.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.120
Why did you leave that?

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.560
The winds blew in a different direction.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:29.220
Really?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.060
How much did you steal?

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.580
It was a long time ago.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.040
And they're gonna welcome the prodigal daughter home with a Thanksgiving meal.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.600
Look, we'll work it out once we're there.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.830
If they've got food, let's go.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.330
What is that appalling smell?

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:46.240
Breakfast.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:48.600
Dentics.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:50.730
Can't eat dentics.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.220
Fried dentics.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.100
Anything if it's fried.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:55.910
I'll pass.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.060
Suit yourself Jenny Craig, but I'm hungry.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.020
Obviously not.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:09.260
That hungry.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.450
I say we starburst out of here and try our luck somewhere else, Crichton.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.680
Aaron, we are out of supplies.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.620
We're going to become the Donner Party of the Uncharted Territories if we don't get some food soon.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.280
Nobody is going to starve.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.030
The colony is food.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:24.320
Gianna's right.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.330
We must go to the mining camp.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:29.090
Of course.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.510
No, Xan, you obviously didn't hear.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.590
Gianna's got enemies that she forgot to tell us about.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.230
I need food now.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:41.400
Xan, what's going on?

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.510
I must have food.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:47.880
We're all done.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:57.290
I'm quite an astronaut.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.970
A radiation wave hit and I got shot through.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:06.090
a wormhole lost in some distant part of the universe on a ship a living ship full of strange

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:12.670
alien life forms help me listen please is there anybody out there who can hear me i'm being hunted

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:19.830
by an insane military commander and everything i can i'm just looking for a way home

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.910
Right, and why? Why do I have to stay aboard Moya?

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:48.750
Because Dargo and I are allergic to whatever's happening to Xan and you aren't.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:53.400
Feeling alright? You up to this?

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:58.140
I'm sure what's worse. The hunger pains are the thrilling allergies!

00:03:58.720 --> 00:03:59.960
What the dren? Now-

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:00.880
What are we waiting for?

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:01.600
Me!

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:02.820
Not me.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:05.220
I am.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.850
You think this will catch Temmin's eye?

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:10.140
Who's Temmin?

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:11.520
Just an odd friend.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.030
He'll look after me.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:14.710
We'll get food.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:15.480
Don't worry.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.320
But we better, or Xan dies.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:19.630
Come on, let's go.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.010
Great, I get to stay on board with the blooming blue bush.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.480
And you get to play with your favorite little trunk.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.190
Back in a couple of orange tops.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.860
Tastes better than this place smells.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.200
What did you expect?

00:04:58.540 --> 00:04:59.140
It's a corpse.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:04:59.980
It's a filthy...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.000
You don't die.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.380
Do you want food or not?

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:07.420
About your friend.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:08.580
Damn it.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.320
What didn't you tell us about him before?

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:15.390
Is he edible?

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:16.910
Shut up, Rigel.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.380
You did, didn't you?

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.620
You stole from this guy.

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:22.370
How's this gonna go down?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:26.440
When I tell him Mary's dead, he'll forget all about the money.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.850
You're gonna use your dead brother to play on his sympathy?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.440
I have a plan.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:35.430
Dargo, it's okay.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:37.270
Chiana has a plan.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:38.750
An attack.

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:39.630
Dargo.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:40.710
Triton.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:41.330
Akiva.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:05.950
This is who's going to help us.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:07.350
Teman.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:09.930
Teman?

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:14.010
Jenna.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:20.780
Jenna, don't let me suffer.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.690
This will get me so good.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:40.770
It's not just you, you're dead anyway!

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.030
Channel, what's happening here?

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:44.330
He smacked!

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:48.420
To a past yule.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.330
Kedva must have been after him.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:54.980
Kedva? What exactly is a Kedva?

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:58.000
Vicious beast that feeds off the Boudon.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.260
Chews up anything...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.020
that gets in the way.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:03.480
You did what needed to be done, Chiana.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:07.440
As usual, these weaklings didn't have the guts

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.700
to put my brother out of his misery.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:14.280
Go home, all of you.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:19.770
I'm closing the mine till I attract that Kiva and kill it.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.330
But with the mines closed,

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:25.310
how are these poor folk gonna earn enough neglect for provisions?

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:29.020
How are you gonna anything if you're dead?

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:31.170
Now, get out of here!

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:31.810
I'm gone.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:33.760
Oh!

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.720
Never thought I'd see you again.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:39.240
You got something new.

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:45.230
Someone used to say you.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:48.980
Wasn't all I liked.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:56.980
Too bad you left so suddenly.

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:01.530
Why are you back?

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:03.450
Our ship's out of food.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:05.690
We're dying of starvation.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:11.600
Thought you could help us out.

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:17.960
You want food?

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:20.200
Hand over your weapons.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:22.070
No.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.110
Then stay hungry.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.180
Here you are, Marshal.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:59.960
Read your friends, but not you.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.310
Luciana, you used up my charity.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:16.000
Get food for Xan.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.100
Alive and kickin'.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.740
Come on, girl, give you a fee.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:51.200
It's Leslie Gopinot.

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:54.430
Oh, Keith, I got her just after you left.

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:57.210
She lost both her arms and half her face.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:58.210
True God.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:09:59.220
To right.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.980
Amara gave it up. She bugged out. She got some kids or something now.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.550
True. What about you?

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:10.260
Scored big and left. Just like I'm about to.

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:16.550
Hey, girl. You've been here too long. You've been waiting your whole life for that big score. No good.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:22.020
No more, girl? I'm leaving. Because I did hit it big.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:34.220
Better shut it before something you won't like flies in.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:38.980
They found something.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:41.790
Vein of negality.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:45.360
Need a second liver just past the ribs.

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:48.160
Set me up for ten lifetimes.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:50.220
I'm so happy for you.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.300
Be happy for yourself, girl.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:53.960
I want you to have a share.

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:55.820
You do?

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.490
Well, then I can get food for a second.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:01.240
For all of us.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:02.760
Just one problem.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:06.030
Basag, that folly, close the mines.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:09.960
Bastards probably down there right now, jumping my claim.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:18.030
Donna, do you think Basag, think Basag could have killed Tevin?

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:19.620
No more, girl.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:20.900
They were brothers.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.960
Surely we can do something, if not cure it, stabilise it.

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:29.830
I can.

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:35.750
Mix a saw, which might slow down the growth of the buds.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:38.150
Great. You stay there and you tell me how to mix it.

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:43.080
Zan, can you tell me?

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:48.580
Gel.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:49.980
Right, and which one are they?

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:53.220
The two marked vials.

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:02.650
Is it supposed to do that?

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:08.620
Sam? Sam? Can you hear me?

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:13.930
Officer Sun?

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:15.620
Yes, what is it, pilot?

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:19.000
The micropollen sand's producing are beginning to affect Moya.

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:22.750
She's experiencing a slight numbing sensation along her inner hull.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.730
It will put the atmosphere scrubbers to maximum capacity.

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:27.090
Already done.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:29.830
Well, I don't know what else to suggest.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.550
This is your grand gesture of generosity.

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:42.770
Fungus, mold, lichens.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:49.090
What's that you're eating?

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:51.160
Meat.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.300
Why didn't I get any meat?

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:54.750
You want meat?

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:56.610
You have to pay for it.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.040
So if what I have given you isn't to your liking...

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:07.380
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:09.740
You can ignore the little green eating machine.

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:11.780
We appreciate what you've done for us.

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:14.920
We need more food.

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:18.190
We need enough to last us until we get to the next system.

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:19.690
You want more?

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:23.060
You have to learn it, like everybody else.

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.980
Once I reopen the mines...

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:27.120
What do you say we trade?

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:29.790
We got medical supplies, weapons...

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.600
This is not a commerce planet. You want meat?

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:39.120
N'gulti crystals bars food, work, gets crystals.

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:40.800
Then we'll work.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:46.290
Dominals do not work, especially not in some rotting corpse filled with creatures.

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:52.030
What are those men doing?

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:55.350
Timo, do you play?

00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:59.920
I'm about to. We're here for Xan.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:01.280
Not games.

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:03.100
I'm here for food.

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:05.420
This is how I'll get it.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:07.440
I'll introduce you.

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:08.830
Most kind.

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:14.130
Maybe we should have fried this.

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:17.460
Well, it ain't lobster, but it'll keep Xan alive.

00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:20.740
Keep an eye on the children till I get back.

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:25.000
Definitely takes the edge off.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.280
Man, could it get any worse in here?

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:28.180
I can barely breathe.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:35.760
Hey, Blue. Delivery. It's not exactly Domino's, but it got here in less than 30 minutes.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:36.650
John.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:56.080
You don't want meat. Meat's bad for you. It's a cholesterol hormone.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:58.360
Animal.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:02.030
Stop the budding cycle.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:05.200
Buds evolved for protection.

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.140
Famine immobilizes us.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:09.700
Predator attacks.

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:11.440
Buds poison animal.

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:15.110
When animal dies, we eat animal.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:38.400
cheated yeah it's part of the game you're just a lousy cheater i'll have you know i am an

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:44.700
excellent cheater i'm just not at my best right now this outrageous hunger is affecting me let's

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:50.260
see some of these neglecty crystals you claim to have we'll settle up when we're done you know what

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:59.550
i think i think you don't have any crystals never did don't be ridiculous you lie about having

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.380
Anything of any value to bet with.

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:06.960
I demand another game, or I'll tear your frelling eyes out.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:10.460
You green-ass, stinking, warty little bastard.

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:11.900
I'm gonna kill you!

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:16.060
That won't get you your crystals.

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:18.280
You'll get me my crystals one way or another.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:23.420
Yeah, you look good on that, Kyle.

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:24.780
You always did.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:33.550
I missed you.

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:40.350
You chose Temmin over me.

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:48.750
Oh, sure, Temmin's gone now.

00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:59.810
You don't seem too broken up about it.

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:01.670
Oh, well, neither do you.

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:04.880
Well, we all grieve in our own way.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:14.360
Taemon was a brother, partner, mission.

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:21.850
We gotta move on.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:23.530
The miners need to...

00:17:23.530 --> 00:17:24.090
BESOG!

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:27.620
Go away!

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:29.910
One of our shipmates has died.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:37.440
she must have meat you have nothing to trade for it we'll get you whatever you want but i want that

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:53.120
meat now there must be something you want is that what this is about free handouts i told you

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:56.300
you want meat you have to pay for it

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:08.050
Maybe you do have something to trade.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:08.630
No!

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:11.920
Does he make all of your decisions for you?

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:14.520
That's not the Tiana I knew.

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:15.510
No.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:18.460
I make my own decisions.

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:26.040
Run away, Luke-san.

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:29.860
Give me what I...

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:39.320
You got me, Vox, Luke-san, but I hid the meat in the mine, and no one knows the mines like I do.

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:45.850
Kill never find it, and your shipmate dies anyway.

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:51.050
He wants a night with me. I'll give it to him.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:58.920
One night? Uh-uh. I play for keeps. A life for a life.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:08.060
I give you meat, you're mine till I'm done with you.

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:11.700
King attacking the fog like that.

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:13.920
What, did you think he'd just hand over the meat?

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:17.960
It seemed like a better idea than waiting for you to frow him into submission.

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:20.440
Yeah, well, if that's what it takes, then that's what it takes.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.860
I thought this was supposed to be about saving Zad.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:25.560
There are other ways to get the crystals that we need.

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:28.000
I will not allow you to stay here with him.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.540
Don't tell me what to do.

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:29.960
Well, someone...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.520
It has to.

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:31.960
Chiana!

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:35.660
Doggo.

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:37.200
I had a brother.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:38.440
He's gone.

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:41.320
Another.

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:44.760
Wanna be your brother?

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:45.870
What?

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:58.490
Do you wanna help?

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:05.360
My friend Altana, she's found this really big vein of crystals.

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:09.980
She's willing to share the wealth.

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:12.660
Is it enough to help save Zan?

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:14.050
More than enough.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.160
Except they closed the mine because of the Kiva.

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:21.240
If I went down there with her.

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:24.190
Calibration is complete.

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:26.870
Did Zan tell you what intent it'd use?

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:29.420
Zan's out of it, pilot. I'm doing this on my own.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.320
Then how do you know it'll help?

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:33.970
I don't, but she's a plant and she loves light.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:52.460
What are you reading, pilot?

00:20:54.740 --> 00:20:58.620
Xan now seems to be exuding spores as a reaction to the intense light.

00:20:59.270 --> 00:20:59.890
Can you do anything?

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:05.920
about it i've minimized moya's ambient illumination as a precaution but the spool levels are still

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:12.040
increasing you've only made things worse i had to do something and you didn't give me any suggestions

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:19.260
why did you do that what i was trying to help them nice you tried to kill me don't be stupid

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:28.340
brutish peacekeeper can't wait to see me die you enjoying it not in the least

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:36.580
Easy? It's never easy.

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:38.680
Boudon.

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:41.850
I'll stay half a cycle. No more.

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:48.990
I've given you my terms. Take them. Or leave them.

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:51.550
That was the deal, Chiana.

00:21:53.590 --> 00:21:54.330
Can't we negotiate?

00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:06.640
Where's Dorgo? Did he get some meat?

00:22:06.830 --> 00:22:08.330
Yeah, he's working on it. In the mines.

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:11.890
What? In the... Is he nuts?

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:14.220
You remember the creature, don't you?

00:22:15.220 --> 00:22:16.280
How long has he been gone?

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:18.400
I don't know. Like three orns or so.

00:22:18.710 --> 00:22:19.550
He's with our turner.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:24.230
It's never easy. I'm gonna go get him.

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:29.980
Zan's spores are spreading faster than the scrubbers can remove it.

00:22:30.090 --> 00:22:34.030
It's penetrating Moya's neural conduits and dulling her senses.

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:34.710
How badly?

00:22:35.180 --> 00:22:37.160
Already enough to impede navigation.

00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:38.060
Can you compensate?

00:22:38.740 --> 00:22:40.550
I'm having difficulty.

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:44.210
My own connection to Moya is still much less than optimal.

00:22:44.950 --> 00:22:46.410
How much damage could these spores do?

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:56.080
If the levels continue to increase, Moya could be permanently blinded.

00:22:56.260 --> 00:22:57.700
It's all right, I won't let that happen, pilot.

00:22:58.380 --> 00:22:59.960
What if Zan were to leave Moya and...

00:23:00.540 --> 00:23:05.100
If she and I were to leave in a transport pod, then you could open the rest of Moira to space and flush the pollen out.

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:15.560
That would help Moira, but what about you? The spores have begun to affect you as well.

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:20.680
No, I'll be fine. We just need to buy some time until Crichton can return with some meat in Prime and Transport Pod, alright?

00:23:21.130 --> 00:23:21.730
Very well.

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:35.600
God pilot

00:24:00.180 --> 00:24:03.080
Rigel, what the hell are you doing down here?

00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:06.220
Get lost, Crichton. This one's mine.

00:24:06.780 --> 00:24:07.460
You seen Dargo?

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:08.760
Forget Dargo.

00:24:09.340 --> 00:24:15.120
That filthy character V-jar threw me down here just because I lost a demo.

00:24:15.780 --> 00:24:16.480
He cheated.

00:24:17.710 --> 00:24:17.950
What?

00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:21.040
Of course I cheated.

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:24.230
Cheated and you lost.

00:24:26.760 --> 00:24:29.460
Dargo and Gianna have a line on some crystals, so let's go.

00:24:30.160 --> 00:24:32.300
Crichton, I've got a crystal right here.

00:24:32.940 --> 00:24:34.280
Our luck is changing.

00:24:34.720 --> 00:24:35.200
Rigor.

00:24:35.770 --> 00:24:35.950
Ow!

00:24:36.660 --> 00:24:37.600
That's your ear, right?

00:24:40.490 --> 00:24:42.100
That is all the time.

00:24:42.900 --> 00:24:45.400
So get your crystal, and let's go!

00:24:45.580 --> 00:24:45.780
Ah!

00:24:46.720 --> 00:24:47.200
Ooh.

00:24:47.480 --> 00:24:47.740
Ooh.

00:26:00.500 --> 00:26:02.460
Get off! Let's go!

00:26:03.040 --> 00:26:06.130
There's no reason for both of us to die!

00:26:06.310 --> 00:26:09.080
I'm a dominar! You're just you!

00:26:09.400 --> 00:26:11.610
Shut your head! And give it more gas!

00:26:11.790 --> 00:26:12.710
There is no more!

00:26:12.910 --> 00:26:14.190
Gas! Let's go!

00:26:16.340 --> 00:26:19.350
You! We're going down! Right now!

00:26:20.080 --> 00:26:23.730
Who am I to God? For the last time!

00:26:25.120 --> 00:26:27.220
Let's go now or I'll bite your fingers off!

00:26:27.360 --> 00:26:28.900
Oh yeah! Screw you!

00:26:43.920 --> 00:26:44.600
I'm looking for you.

00:26:47.320 --> 00:26:49.920
I hate your lunch.

00:26:50.560 --> 00:26:51.920
Dentix tasted better.

00:26:52.990 --> 00:26:53.870
You tasted worse.

00:27:01.240 --> 00:27:05.320
You're going to go back to the transport pod and stay there.

00:27:05.950 --> 00:27:07.010
What about Veja?

00:27:07.660 --> 00:27:08.970
What about Kiva?

00:27:09.460 --> 00:27:11.060
Oh, good plan.

00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:38.080
Zan? Zan! Why won't you answer me?

00:27:39.420 --> 00:27:41.120
Pilot, why can't you locate her?

00:27:41.320 --> 00:27:44.280
The spores have clouded Moya's senses too much.

00:27:44.720 --> 00:27:46.520
I can't even track who you are.

00:27:47.080 --> 00:27:49.380
I'm on Tier 7 and there's no sign of Zan.

00:27:50.550 --> 00:27:52.400
This is soon. Moya's worsening.

00:27:52.690 --> 00:27:56.570
If we don't find Zan soon, we may have to flush the atmosphere anyway.

00:27:58.290 --> 00:27:58.750
Understood.

00:28:21.240 --> 00:28:22.520
I wouldn't have done this without you.

00:28:22.980 --> 00:28:24.480
Both our purposes are served.

00:28:25.610 --> 00:28:27.410
We save Xan, and you get out of here.

00:28:28.260 --> 00:28:29.980
I'm not gonna miss the stan-

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:32.580
I'll miss this thrill of it.

00:28:35.690 --> 00:28:39.120
Always living constantly on your guard.

00:28:40.210 --> 00:28:41.370
And live and fighting.

00:28:41.590 --> 00:28:43.910
You sound like Jenna.

00:28:44.530 --> 00:28:45.350
Oh, that girl.

00:28:45.970 --> 00:28:47.470
She's a wild one.

00:28:49.240 --> 00:28:51.900
Let go.

00:28:53.680 --> 00:28:55.640
Tees are certainly flexible, that's for sure.

00:28:56.470 --> 00:28:59.830
She'll do whatever it takes to get meat for your friends.

00:29:00.480 --> 00:29:09.800
is me. Nah, we always came out on top the two of us. We had our fun even when she and Temmin were

00:29:09.800 --> 00:29:17.760
together. That fella, he was good for her and her brother. Yet she repays his kindness by stealing

00:29:17.760 --> 00:29:29.980
from him. That's why it's very difficult to trust her. Darga, you and...

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:35.790
Tiana together, no or not yet.

00:29:40.470 --> 00:29:40.910
Duh.

00:29:44.090 --> 00:29:48.490
Erin, any further deterioration and Moya will lose all ability to navigate.

00:29:49.690 --> 00:29:51.070
Though we can't wait any longer.

00:29:51.730 --> 00:29:56.370
But unless Zan secured herself in a transport pod, decompression will kill her.

00:29:57.640 --> 00:29:59.200
There's no other way to save Moya.

00:30:03.260 --> 00:30:04.800
Then seal of command and do it.

00:30:11.260 --> 00:30:13.830
Decompression and five microns.

00:30:30.800 --> 00:30:31.260
Thank you, boss.

00:30:37.190 --> 00:30:37.890
Officer, soon.

00:30:39.070 --> 00:30:40.250
All levels have dropped.

00:30:41.320 --> 00:30:41.800
Thank you, pilot.

00:30:43.660 --> 00:30:45.460
Beginning repressurization now.

00:30:46.600 --> 00:30:47.680
It'll take over an hour.

00:31:32.040 --> 00:31:32.940
Dargo make it back?

00:31:33.250 --> 00:31:34.050
Well, didn't you find it?

00:31:34.470 --> 00:31:38.560
No, I found Rigel and one very big, ugly critter.

00:31:38.740 --> 00:31:40.200
They should be back by now with the crystals.

00:31:40.840 --> 00:31:43.140
It's been a hell of a day.

00:31:43.810 --> 00:31:45.850
If we don't get some meat before the end of it,

00:31:45.910 --> 00:31:48.290
I'm gonna cut my own damn arm off and feed it to Xan.

00:31:51.120 --> 00:31:51.740
It's your alarm.

00:31:53.320 --> 00:31:53.640
Altana.

00:31:55.730 --> 00:31:56.270
What happened?

00:31:57.560 --> 00:31:58.700
Lines were claws.

00:31:59.160 --> 00:31:59.980
But some of you...

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:07.720
decided to ignore that. Where's Dargo on Eltona? I found your friends, but got there too late.

00:32:08.160 --> 00:32:13.380
What the hell do you mean too late? I heard the keeper and drove it off.

00:32:14.160 --> 00:32:24.780
Drawn! Drawn! Dargo! Easy, try to get it.

00:33:00.120 --> 00:33:01.350
I can just stop.

00:33:02.530 --> 00:33:03.290
How bad you hurt?

00:33:04.610 --> 00:33:05.570
Nothing broken.

00:33:05.910 --> 00:33:06.870
Blood's running clear.

00:33:07.550 --> 00:33:08.250
I'll survive.

00:33:09.260 --> 00:33:11.040
Your friend's lucky to be alive.

00:33:11.480 --> 00:33:12.340
How could this happen?

00:33:12.720 --> 00:33:14.660
First him and now Altona.

00:33:15.370 --> 00:33:18.610
You know what, Boudreau, for someone that's supposed to be such a great critter hunter,

00:33:18.770 --> 00:33:20.290
you ain't doing that good of a job.

00:33:21.740 --> 00:33:23.780
I closed the mines for a reason.

00:33:24.080 --> 00:33:27.320
Now stay out and let me do what I have to do.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:33.620
All right, Pip. What's the plan now?

00:33:34.830 --> 00:33:38.520
He killed Ultano. He's gonna go steal her crystals. I'm not gonna let him.

00:33:39.650 --> 00:33:42.540
You stay here with Dargo. Boudreau is mine.

00:33:50.950 --> 00:33:52.010
How much longer, pilot?

00:33:53.240 --> 00:33:56.560
Repressurization will be complete in 900 microns.

00:34:06.060 --> 00:34:18.620
Dan, you don't understand.

00:34:21.020 --> 00:34:25.990
To kill me, suffocate me, poison Sal, burn me with light.

00:34:26.310 --> 00:34:28.390
I've only been trying to help you.

00:34:29.200 --> 00:34:29.500
No.

00:34:30.160 --> 00:34:30.660
I always hated.

00:34:31.810 --> 00:34:32.690
Came to Delvia.

00:34:33.750 --> 00:34:34.510
Imprisoned me.

00:34:34.970 --> 00:34:35.390
Zad?

00:34:35.960 --> 00:34:36.940
They were peacekeepers.

00:34:37.500 --> 00:34:39.120
I'm no longer a peacekeeper.

00:34:39.660 --> 00:34:41.000
Always a peacekeeper.

00:34:42.620 --> 00:34:43.460
Our barracks.

00:34:46.580 --> 00:34:47.860
Afraid to come near me.

00:34:49.640 --> 00:34:50.700
Afraid of contaminating.

00:34:51.460 --> 00:34:52.000
Not true.

00:34:52.440 --> 00:34:53.950
Putting a pilot against me.

00:34:55.610 --> 00:34:55.850
Death.

00:34:56.580 --> 00:34:57.940
Nobody wanted you dead.

00:34:58.460 --> 00:34:59.980
We did whatever we could to help you.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:01.700
but we ran out of options.

00:35:02.120 --> 00:35:04.420
Your spores are harming Moya.

00:35:05.220 --> 00:35:06.320
Would never harm Moya.

00:35:06.580 --> 00:35:08.870
San, look at me.

00:35:09.740 --> 00:35:10.560
Barely talk.

00:35:10.780 --> 00:35:12.040
I could barely breathe properly.

00:35:12.560 --> 00:35:13.560
Your spores are doing that,

00:35:13.600 --> 00:35:14.980
and it's far worse for Moya.

00:35:15.740 --> 00:35:21.320
Moya, life defuse me.

00:35:21.630 --> 00:35:23.510
No, I'm trying to get through to you,

00:35:23.570 --> 00:35:25.410
and for the sake of your goddess, think.

00:35:30.280 --> 00:35:30.620
Think.

00:35:32.020 --> 00:35:32.540
Hazy.

00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:35.110
Look for the haze, Anne.

00:35:36.010 --> 00:35:36.170
Think.

00:35:36.770 --> 00:35:38.670
You're a Dolby and 10th level pal.

00:35:38.890 --> 00:35:40.750
You trade your mind to control your thoughts.

00:35:40.970 --> 00:35:41.670
Do it now.

00:35:43.180 --> 00:35:43.740
I will.

00:36:08.570 --> 00:36:08.930
Pilot.

00:36:09.130 --> 00:36:09.630
Yes?

00:36:10.120 --> 00:36:12.080
The transport pod pried.

00:37:04.920 --> 00:37:06.120
Nice stash you got here.

00:37:08.220 --> 00:37:10.060
Came down to steal some of it.

00:37:11.290 --> 00:37:13.030
No, fella, you have to earn it.

00:37:13.320 --> 00:37:15.700
Like Altana was doing before the critter got her.

00:37:17.950 --> 00:37:19.330
Speak of the devil.

00:37:19.430 --> 00:37:21.350
When do you say we take this conversation someplace else?

00:37:22.190 --> 00:37:22.430
No.

00:37:28.680 --> 00:37:29.400
Somewhere before.

00:37:32.880 --> 00:37:33.500
Not yet.

00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:35.820
And I've seen this guy somewhere before.

00:37:39.340 --> 00:37:43.770
It's a primitive animal, but intelligent in its own way.

00:37:44.880 --> 00:37:50.120
Over the years, we have developed a mutually beneficial relationship.

00:37:50.500 --> 00:37:52.780
Well, I'm really not interested in your personal life.

00:37:54.170 --> 00:37:57.580
And I should warn you, it tastes too good.

00:37:58.280 --> 00:37:59.260
They won't eat you.

00:38:00.190 --> 00:38:02.230
He prefers what I give him.

00:38:02.990 --> 00:38:06.820
That's how I trained him to have his way.

00:38:07.740 --> 00:38:14.920
I'll let you two get to know each other.

00:38:15.300 --> 00:38:21.430
Dog, right?

00:38:21.730 --> 00:38:24.190
What I got?

00:38:27.800 --> 00:38:28.900
Yeah, this is good, huh?

00:38:30.120 --> 00:38:30.740
I want this, yeah?

00:38:31.020 --> 00:38:31.240
Yeah.

00:38:36.380 --> 00:38:37.120
Good boy.

00:38:37.340 --> 00:38:38.060
Good boy.

00:40:31.340 --> 00:40:32.180
Get away!

00:40:36.716 --> 00:40:37.236
Where's Creighton?

00:40:37.996 --> 00:40:39.096
I have no idea.

00:40:39.692 --> 00:40:41.272
Don't thrill with me.

00:40:41.452 --> 00:40:42.092
Believe me.

00:40:42.604 --> 00:40:43.404
I'll believe you.

00:40:43.852 --> 00:40:45.852
Well, that's a joke get him up

00:40:48.780 --> 00:40:49.340
Yeah, I know.

00:40:50.828 --> 00:40:51.828
You're a thief!

00:40:51.828 --> 00:40:52.828
Find a truck!

00:40:52.844 --> 00:40:53.684
But you're not a killer.

00:40:55.500 --> 00:40:56.780
I'm evolving as air.

00:40:57.548 --> 00:40:58.248
As an individual.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:00.700
I know you.

00:41:02.172 --> 00:41:03.892
You won't shoot me in cold blood.

00:41:04.924 --> 00:41:06.164
You can't do it.

00:42:02.200 --> 00:42:02.380
Yeah?

00:42:02.500 --> 00:42:02.800
What?

00:42:02.980 --> 00:42:03.320
No.

00:42:03.970 --> 00:42:04.890
That was your fourth plate.

00:42:05.130 --> 00:42:05.310
Oh.

00:42:05.670 --> 00:42:09.230
There you go.

00:42:09.390 --> 00:42:09.880
Thank you.

00:42:10.020 --> 00:42:10.900
Another helping?

00:42:15.540 --> 00:42:28.470
no it's wonderful yeah carolina style keith best barbecue this side of a budong

00:42:30.764 --> 00:42:31.984
Thank you, John, for everything.

00:42:31.984 --> 00:42:32.124
My pleasure.

00:42:32.972 --> 00:42:33.732
Y'all do good now.

00:42:34.284 --> 00:42:35.124
Mm-hmm.

00:42:39.692 --> 00:42:41.692
The pilot is very relieved that you're recovering.

00:42:45.164 --> 00:42:47.524
As much as I suffered, your experience was...

00:42:48.588 --> 00:42:50.948
It was also painful. I only made it more difficult for you.

00:42:51.788 --> 00:42:52.748
You weren't yourself, son.

00:42:54.732 --> 00:42:57.232
No, I was the mindless savage I accused you of being.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:02.800
It wasn't very pleasant reverting back to such a primitive.

00:43:04.156 --> 00:43:05.496
Vicious state, I...

00:43:06.844 --> 00:43:07.844
Sorry for what I said.

00:43:09.340 --> 00:43:09.600
Yeah.

00:43:11.004 --> 00:43:11.364
Eat.

00:43:12.572 --> 00:43:13.572
Don't talk.

00:43:30.350 --> 00:43:31.290
Be happy to be out of there.

00:43:34.520 --> 00:43:35.780
Can't understand, oh God.

00:43:38.460 --> 00:43:40.980
Understand what, boss?

00:43:44.140 --> 00:43:44.860
Understand that?

00:43:46.760 --> 00:43:47.520
It's not a big thing.

00:43:52.060 --> 00:43:55.390
Can't have an act for me.

00:43:57.760 --> 00:43:58.820
Do what I do to survive.

00:44:00.760 --> 00:44:01.860
Can't you just let it go?

00:44:03.730 --> 00:44:04.900
I'm gonna let go safe.

00:44:06.650 --> 00:44:07.350
You are safe.

00:44:10.840 --> 00:44:11.160
Am I?
